From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:18:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: keep BC raw blocks only after the device reads one
 back

csf-v11/201 gave every readable (TRANSFER_SRC) BC lowmem image a raw
store, and 203 made every upload write the raw blocks next to the
transcode: one more write of the source size per upload, a BO per full
upload (memset on the CPU) and a spill to flash later. DXVK sets
TRANSFER_SRC on nearly every texture but almost never reads one back.
RC4-lowmem and the GunaCharanTeja fork keep no raw blocks at all.

PANVK_BC_RAW=lazy (the new default): readable 2D BC1-BC5 images (ETC2/EAC
shadows) created before the device ever read a BC image back keep no
raw blocks (bc_raw_lazy, with bc_no_raw). Uploads write only the shadow.
A BC -> BC vkCmdCopyImage from such an image into one with the same
shadow format copies the shadow blocks (panvk_bc_scopy.comp), which is
exact for sampling. Any other read of its raw blocks (copy to a
buffer or memory, copy to a non-BC image) is skipped with one warning
and sets the device's bc_raw.needed, so BC images created after it get a
raw store again and read back exactly. BC6H/BC7 and 3D images keep
their raw stores.

PANVK_BC_RAW=store restores csf-v11/201-206 (a raw store for every
readable image), PANVK_BC_RAW=plane the raw plane in the image memory.
Apps that check raw readback bit-exactly (PanProbe bc_decode) set
PANVK_BC_RAW=store.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
